(422298, 37734, 8522, '<td valign="top">Attention to detail may have helped you here:<br/>1: Spelling.<br/>2: Straighten your horizon.<br/>3: Your picture is WAY too small. Ask in the forums for help on submitting a decent sized image.<br/> <br/>This may have been an interesting picture otherwise, but it''s hard to tell. 4</td>', 'Attention to detail may have helped you here:1: Spelling.2: Straighten your horizon.3: Your picture is WAY too small. Ask in the forums for help on submitting a decent sized image. This may have been an interesting picture otherwise, but it''s hard to tell. 4', '2003-09-17 20:06:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(422301, 38150, 8522, '<td valign="top">I hate to be mean, but I''ve seen this setup on DPC quite a few times now, and it''s starting to become pretty unoriginal. The advice seems to be to overexpose a few stops when shooting white paper, so your text stands out better and the contrast is improved. The particular text used for this challenge is a nice touch though. Perhaps you could have used these printed words from a different viewing angle, or doing something different with the paper? I think it''s a shame that there''s a space around the word ''LIVING?'', I''d have prefered the rest of the text right up to it, perhaps ''LIVING?'' could have been in another colour. 5</td>', 'I hate to be mean, but I''ve seen this setup on DPC quite a few times now, and it''s starting to become pretty unoriginal. The advice seems to be to overexpose a few stops when shooting white paper, so your text stands out better and the contrast is improved. The particular text used for this challenge is a nice touch though. Perhaps you could have used these printed words from a different viewing angle, or doing something different with the paper? I think it''s a shame that there''s a space around the word ''LIVING?'', I''d have prefered the rest of the text right up to it, perhaps ''LIVING?'' could have been in another colour. 5', '2003-09-17 20:11:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(422304, 37434, 8522, '<td valign="top">WOW!<br/>Congrats on your new arrival, what an amazing photo.<br/>The skin is so smooth... not having seen a newborn, did it really look like this, or is this the result of NeatImage?<br/>The composition doesn''t give me enough of a wow factor for a 10, but then I''m not sure photography would have been my first concern in your position. 8</td>', 'WOW!Congrats on your new arrival, what an amazing photo.The skin is so smooth... not having seen a newborn, did it really look like this, or is this the result of NeatImage?The composition doesn''t give me enough of a wow factor for a 10, but then I''m not sure photography would have been my first concern in your position. 8', '2003-09-17 20:17:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(422313, 38082, 8522, '<td valign="top">VERY interesting... shame about the glare from the marble. Makes me ponder a lot, this one. Great lighting, wonderful concept. I''d have perhaps liked a blue/green marble. A good take on the challenge. 8</td>', 'VERY interesting... shame about the glare from the marble. Makes me ponder a lot, this one. Great lighting, wonderful concept. I''d have perhaps liked a blue/green marble. A good take on the challenge. 8', '2003-09-17 20:27:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(422314, 38019, 8522, '<td valign="top">Perhaps this is being picky, but I can''t think of anything more lifeless and barren than the moon. Nice shot though! 4</td>', 'Perhaps this is being picky, but I can''t think of anything more lifeless and barren than the moon. Nice shot though! 4', '2003-09-17 20:29:07.000000', NULL, 1),
