(424269, 38185, 6999, '<td valign="top">Such an odd photograph - here''s a few things that stike me about it. Composition - mt eye is constantly drawn to the shadows, rather than the subject. The real contrat lines are hugel exaggerated by over-sharpening (check where the two apples overlap). Graininess: the red field is enormously speckled, and that persists in the apples - there''s no texture there at all! Low cantrast - there''s no white, no  black: given the muted subject, that at leasst would be neccesary to proveide some purely visulal interest. <br/> <br/>What''s more annoying is that it''s a prety good idea - just that it could have been executed so much better. It needs composition, texture, depth, and prbably a kore intersting view-point. especially with one seed sitting on the surfacr of the apple: imagine a low level shot of that, against a dark background, with the seed picked out by lighting from the rear and the side ... you''d have a winner there.</td>', 'Such an odd photograph - here''s a few things that stike me about it. Composition - mt eye is constantly drawn to the shadows, rather than the subject. The real contrat lines are hugel exaggerated by over-sharpening (check where the two apples overlap). Graininess: the red field is enormously speckled, and that persists in the apples - there''s no texture there at all! Low cantrast - there''s no white, no  black: given the muted subject, that at leasst would be neccesary to proveide some purely visulal interest.  What''s more annoying is that it''s a prety good idea - just that it could have been executed so much better. It needs composition, texture, depth, and prbably a kore intersting view-point. especially with one seed sitting on the surfacr of the apple: imagine a low level shot of that, against a dark background, with the seed picked out by lighting from the rear and the side ... you''d have a winner there.', '2003-09-19 19:46:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(424271, 37779, 4411, '<td valign="top">And the award for most bizarre photo of the challenge goes to ...<br/> <br/>The sky is blown out to heck but nevermind, a funny and well composed photo from a twisted mind : )</td>', 'And the award for most bizarre photo of the challenge goes to ... The sky is blown out to heck but nevermind, a funny and well composed photo from a twisted mind : )', '2003-09-19 20:01:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(424272, 38081, 9481, '<td valign="top">This photo would look better with something to hold it together on the left.  Maybe put the candles in a straighter arrangement too.</td>', 'This photo would look better with something to hold it together on the left.  Maybe put the candles in a straighter arrangement too.', '2003-09-19 20:09:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(424279, 37545, 7350, '<td valign="top">This is a fantastic shot.  The white around the edges suggest that it is a photograph of a photograph, though.  Is that right?</td>', 'This is a fantastic shot.  The white around the edges suggest that it is a photograph of a photograph, though.  Is that right?', '2003-09-19 20:50:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(424292, 38040, 11800, '<td valign="top">Yes. She does look like she is enjoying life. Love the sparkle and the feeling that she just said something amusing.</td>', 'Yes. She does look like she is enjoying life. Love the sparkle and the feeling that she just said something amusing.', '2003-09-19 21:35:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(424312, 37503, 11800, '<td valign="top">Soft. But otherwise good comp and I like the b/w treatment,</td>', 'Soft. But otherwise good comp and I like the b/w treatment,', '2003-09-19 21:55:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(424315, 38170, 11800, '<td valign="top">They are charming. Can''t help but smile along with them.</td>', 'They are charming. Can''t help but smile along with them.', '2003-09-19 22:00:34.000000', NULL, 1),
