(428577, 38154, 12268, '<td valign="top">Hey,<br/>I really liked your picture for the life challenge. I think it was the best.<br/></td>', 'Hey,I really liked your picture for the life challenge. I think it was the best.', '2003-09-24 13:30:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(428581, 37305, 11157, '<td valign="top">I like it.</td>', 'I like it.', '2003-09-24 13:32:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(428595, 38155, 12268, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vtruan:</b></div><hr/><i>IMO you needed to back off a bit.  Blown up this much really doesn''t show the real baby you want to portray, it looks very squeezed in.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hey Thanks for your comments! I''m fairly new at all this. What is IMO? I''m not shure why it came out so pixellated. I didn''t crop or enlarge it. The yellowish tint came from not using a flash. The 5050 is notorious for doing this (I''ve read).<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by vtruan:IMO you needed to back off a bit.  Blown up this much really doesn''t show the real baby you want to portray, it looks very squeezed in.  Hey Thanks for your comments! I''m fairly new at all this. What is IMO? I''m not shure why it came out so pixellated. I didn''t crop or enlarge it. The yellowish tint came from not using a flash. The 5050 is notorious for doing this (I''ve read).', '2003-09-24 13:35:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(428606, 38155, 12268, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by xhoss:</b></div><hr/><i>pixelated...did you use the digital zoom or resize?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I can''t remember if I used zoom or not, but the pic was not enlarged or cropped. I tried to sharpen it a little &amp; I think I list a bit in doing so. I took the picture with a high resolution thereby making the size much bigger. Thanks for your comments. It will help in my future picutres &amp; correcting some of the problems I had with this one.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by xhoss:pixelated...did you use the digital zoom or resize?  I can''t remember if I used zoom or not, but the pic was not enlarged or cropped. I tried to sharpen it a little & I think I list a bit in doing so. I took the picture with a high resolution thereby making the size much bigger. Thanks for your comments. It will help in my future picutres & correcting some of the problems I had with this one.', '2003-09-24 13:37:45.000000', NULL, 0),
